Task: Machine-specific value sweep

What was searched: every tracked file, for absolute paths under a home
directory, for this machine's account name, for the directory the drawing
application was built in, and for the binary being invoked by a fixed name.

What was found: no absolute paths and no account name anywhere - the repository
was already clean on that count. Three real findings instead:

1. The user-local package tree was located by twenty duplicated lines in the
   test runner and in both check commands, with the interpreter version written
   into six paths by hand. Replaced by one helper that reads the version from
   the interpreter.

2. Three commands written in the process and stack documents invoked the
   drawing application by a fixed name instead of the environment variable the
   same document defines for it. Corrected.

3. One of those documented commands pointed at a script path that does not
   exist - it named the core runner where it meant the runtime one. Corrected.

Also brought the track's recorded status into line with reality.

Gates after the sweep: 78 unit tests pass, 29 runtime checks pass inside the
real application, linter and formatter clean across 30 files, core layer clean,
core coverage 100 percent.
